WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
Is Japanese skincare better than Korean skincare?

00:00:02.261 --> 00:00:03.461
Let's. Let's talk about it.

00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:06.821
Japanese skincare reminds me a lot of French pharmacy.

00:00:06.822 --> 00:00:09.821
Is very much built around science and prevention.

00:00:09.822 --> 00:00:10.981
It feels more clinical.

00:00:10.982 --> 00:00:14.661
Japanese brands mostly design their products to be used consistently

00:00:14.662 --> 00:00:17.501
every single day for a really long time

00:00:17.502 --> 00:00:20.861
before launching the next big new product that you must have.

00:00:20.862 --> 00:00:23.061
Once something works, it stays the same.

00:00:23.062 --> 00:00:25.861
It becomes iconic staple for so many people.

00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:26.541
And that's why, to me,

00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:28.481
often feels like French pharmacy.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.760
Um, clinical,

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.920
somewhat, um, sensible, quiet,

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.340
not really trend driven, but driven by science and innovation

00:00:36.341 --> 00:00:37.461
still at the same time.

00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:40.501
I would say a lot of the Japanese products are very dependable.

00:00:40.502 --> 00:00:41.841
If you love a product,

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.340
you're probably gonna be able to use that product

00:00:43.341 --> 00:00:44.261
for the next 10 years

00:00:44.262 --> 00:00:46.861
without a reformulation or without it disappearing.

00:00:46.862 --> 00:00:49.501
Korean skincare, in my opinion,

00:00:49.502 --> 00:00:52.021
comes from a much more different approach.

00:00:52.022 --> 00:00:55.501
It's more innovation LED and consumer responsive.

00:00:55.502 --> 00:00:57.741
With some very, very good marketing.

00:00:57.742 --> 00:01:00.061
These brands move extremely quickly.

00:01:00.062 --> 00:01:02.221
They're very good at listening to customer feedback,

00:01:02.222 --> 00:01:05.461
and they aren't afraid to experiment with different ingredients.

00:01:05.462 --> 00:01:08.261
Of ingredients that don't have complete scientific backing yet.

00:01:08.262 --> 00:01:09.981
New textures, formats,

00:01:09.982 --> 00:01:11.901
categories of skincare products.

00:01:11.902 --> 00:01:14.081
You know that we seen it all from K Beauty.

00:01:14.082 --> 00:01:17.021
And that's why so many things that we consider normal now,

00:01:17.022 --> 00:01:18.501
like essences, um,

00:01:18.502 --> 00:01:19.661
sheet masks, ampoules,

00:01:19.662 --> 00:01:23.361
and not just serums, are now so mainstream everywhere else.

00:01:23.362 --> 00:01:24.141
And I've seen people Say

00:01:24.142 --> 00:01:27.141
Japanese skincare is more reliable a fair few times,

00:01:27.142 --> 00:01:28.821
to be honest with you. And I do get it.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.341
I get it. It's almost, like,

00:01:30.342 --> 00:01:32.821
built to be boring in the best possible way

00:01:32.822 --> 00:01:34.821
because it doesn't need a lot of fancy stuff.

00:01:34.822 --> 00:01:36.861
And I feel like it's also reflected in the packaging.

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:39.541
It feels very clinical. One is about the less is more approach,

00:01:39.542 --> 00:01:40.621
your good old dependables.

00:01:40.622 --> 00:01:44.741
And one is about evolving as quickly as the fast paced beauty industry.

00:01:44.742 --> 00:01:46.501
And honestly, the best skincare routines,

00:01:46.502 --> 00:01:49.801
I honestly feel, borrow a little bit from both of these philosophies.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.020
I like the dependability,

00:01:51.021 --> 00:01:53.261
but I also like the skin entertainment at the same time.

00:01:53.262 --> 00:01:53.621
But yeah,

00:01:53.622 --> 00:01:55.503
if you want some J. Beauty recommendations, let me
